        91.200000000000003,
        462.86810000000003,
        410.19299999999993,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 464,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 7,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5937
      },
      "text" : "two national ACH operators. As an ACH operator, the Reserve Banks receive files of payments"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        446.86810000000003,
        425.1939999999999,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 464,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 7,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5937
      },
      "text" : "from originating institutions, edit and sort the payments, deliver the payments to receiving institu-"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        430.86810000000003,
        425.64299999999963,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 464,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 7,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5937
      },
      "text" : "tions, and settle the payments by crediting and debiting the institutions’ accounts. Unlike Fedwire"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        414.86810000000003,
        420.14599999999967,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 464,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 7,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5937
      },
      "text" : "transfers, which are processed and settled immediately, ACH transactions are value-dated—that"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        398.86810000000003,
        423.69199999999984,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 464,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 7,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5937
      },
      "text" : "is, the originator of the ACH transaction includes the settlement date in the payment instructions"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        382.86810000000003,
        156.60000000000002,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 464,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 7,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5937
      },
      "text" : "when they originate the transaction."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        350.86810000000003,
        401.79299999999984,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 465,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 4,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5938
      },
      "text" : "In the past, the United States had several regional ACH systems, but over time, the industry"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        334.86810000000003,
        422.79199999999986,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 465,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 4,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5938
      },
      "text" : "consolidated to the current structure of two national ACH systems. In 2019, the Federal Reserve"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        318.86810000000003,
        421.39500000000004,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 465,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 4,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5938
      },
      "text" : "processed more than 15.5 billion commercial ACH payments, worth approximately $28.1 trillion,"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        302.86810000000003,
        380.99599999999998,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 465,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 4,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5938
      },
      "text" : "and more than 1.7 billion government ACH payments, worth approximately $5.8 trillion."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        270.86810000000003,
        432.04799999999972,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 466,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 2,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5939
      },
      "text" : "The ACH was originally designed to help automate recurring payments, such as government benefit"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        91.200000000000003,
        254.86810000000003,
        412.09499999999963,
        11.639999999999986
      ],
      "structure" : {
        "group" : 466,
        "headingLevel" : 0,
        "lineCount" : 2,
        "opensWithSplitMarker" : false,
        "order" : 5939
      },
      "text" : "payments, payroll payments, and consumer mortgage and utility payments. Much of the recent"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 10,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.7,
        203.74010000000001,
        266.19599999999997,
        11.840000000000003
      ],
      "text" : "Figure 6.5. Examples of automated clearinghouse transfers"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 8,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.7,
        186.75220000000002,
        403.2727999999999,
        9.3120000000000118
      ],
      "text" : "Automated clearinghouse (ACH) transfers can be categorized as either “credit transfers” or “debit transfers” based"
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 8,
      "monospaced" : false,
      "rect" : [
        103.7,
        176.75220000000002,
        218.07599999999996,
        9.3120000000000118
      ],
      "text" : "on the type of instruction sent by the originator of the transfer."
    },
    {
      "fontSize" : 8,
